{{also|Royalty}}
==English==

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|royaltee}}, {{m|enm|roialtee}}, {{m|enm|royalte}}, from {{der|en|fro|roialté}}, {{m|fro|roiauté}}, {{m|fro|realté}} (compare earlier {{cog|fro|realted|t=realm, kingdom}}), from {{der|en|VL.|*rēgālitās}}, from {{der|en|la|rēgālis}}, equivalent to {{af|en|royal|-ty}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈɹɔɪəlti/|a=UK}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-royalty.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# The [[rank]], [[status]], [[power]] or [[authority]] of a monarch.
# People of [[royal]] [[rank]], plus their [[families]], treated as a [[group]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2022 December 14|author=Robin Leleux|title=A royal occasion as heritage projects honoured: Wolferton|journal=RAIL|issue=972|page=61|text=Wolferton was an important station on the Kings Lynn-Hunstanton line, which closed in 1969. As the station was convenient for the Sandringham estate, it was regularly patronised by '''royalty''', and royal retiring rooms were provided.}}
# A royal [[right]] or [[prerogative]], such as the [[exploitation]] of a [[natural resource]]; the [[granting]] of such a right; [[payment]] received for such a right.
# The payment received by an owner of real property for exploitation of [[mineral right]]s in the property.
# {{lb|en|by extension}} Payment made to a [[writer]], [[composer]], [[inventor]] etc for the [[sale]] or [[use]] of [[intellectual property]], [[invention]] etc.
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} Someone in a privileged position.
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Daniel Taylor|title=England humiliated as Iceland knock them out of Euro 2016|url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2016/jun/27/england-iceland-euro-2016-match-report|newspaper=w:The Guardian|location=London|date=27 June 2016|passage=England will have another manager for the next World Cup, Hodgson’s reign will be defined by a result comparable to losing to the United States in the 1950 World Cup and the now-familiar inquest will begin again in a country that likes to see itself as football '''royalty'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en-US|author=Theodore Schleifer|title=How Biden Lost George Clooney and Hollywood|work=The New York Times|date=2024-07-11|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2024/07/11/us/politics/biden-george-clooney-hollywood.html|issn=0362-4331|author2=Jacob Bernstein|author3=Reid J. Epstein|passage=The Biden large-donor scene, where Mr. Katzenberg is treated as '''royalty''' himself, has been devastated since Mr. Biden’s debate performance two weeks ago. }}
# {{lb|en|poker|slang}} A [[king]] and a [[queen]] as a starting hand in [[Texas hold 'em]].
# {{lb|en|Scotland|historical}} The [[bounds]] of a [[royal burgh]].

